1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,460
Hi, I'm Henry.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,096
This is Beezy: an AI operations team for small businesses,

3
00:00:05,136 --> 00:00:06,789
built on Meta's Muse Spark.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,933
Small business owners like Mia run everything across tools

5
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:14,723
that never talk to each other: a stock spreadsheet,

6
00:00:14,763 --> 00:00:17,842
supplier emails, a payroll calculator, a contract folder.

7
00:00:17,882 --> 00:00:20,139
Problems show up after they've cost money.

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,730
Beezy gives her six AI departments.

9
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,939
They spot problems, prepare the work, and then they wait.

10
00:00:25,979 --> 00:00:29,036
Nothing that spends money happens without her approval.

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,411
An Executive Assistant on Muse Spark plans each

12
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:37,287
request and consults specialist agents in parallel.

13
00:00:37,327 --> 00:00:39,261
Their tools run deterministic code,

14
00:00:39,301 --> 00:00:41,855
so the model decides but never does the maths.

15
00:00:41,895 --> 00:00:43,829
And a verifier checks every figure.

16
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,192
Mia signs in to a morning briefing that pulls the

17
00:00:50,232 --> 00:00:54,501
key numbers from every department, each one checked against her records.

18
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:01,054
She asks for a health check.

19
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:05,525
The Executive Assistant decides which departments it needs, and you can

20
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:09,052
watch each one work through real tool calls on her data.

21
00:01:09,092 --> 00:01:10,816
She gets a short summary and

22
00:01:10,856 --> 00:01:13,083
visual cards built from her records.

23
00:01:18,330 --> 00:01:20,879
Here's that request as Muse Spark sees it.

24
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:23,900
Six agents are offered as tools, Muse Spark calls

25
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:26,797
them in parallel, and the real data flows back.

26
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:29,324
Voice commands use Muse Voice Transcribe.

27
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:33,332
Now one tap asks it to act:

28
00:01:33,372 --> 00:01:35,502
restock everything that's running low.

29
00:01:35,542 --> 00:01:39,671
The Procurement agent drafts three purchase orders, but only drafts them.

30
00:01:39,711 --> 00:01:42,870
One click on Approve all, and they're sent to suppliers.

31
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:45,040
In this version, sending is simulated.

32
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:48,250
Why Highland Roasters and not the cheaper supplier?

33
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:50,198
The cheaper one can't deliver before

34
00:01:50,238 --> 00:01:51,875
the beans run out in four days.

35
00:01:51,915 --> 00:01:54,040
That comparison is plain, testable code.

36
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:57,182
Every contract deadline sits on one timeline,

37
00:01:57,222 --> 00:01:58,916
with notice deadlines in red.

38
00:01:58,956 --> 00:02:02,386
She drops in a new pastry contract, and the Contract agent

39
00:02:02,426 --> 00:02:06,214
pulls out the terms and the notice clause, with page references.

40
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:12,300
Payroll is calculated in code, never by the model,

41
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:17,076
and it flags problems before payday: one missing timesheet, one missing bank account.

42
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:19,298
Automations react on their own.

43
00:02:19,338 --> 00:02:21,635
When oat milk drops below twenty percent,

44
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:24,771
a purchase order is drafted for approval straight away.

45
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,893
Each rule shows exactly how it works,

46
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:31,702
and every one ends with the owner approving.

47
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,874
That's what makes it trustworthy: verified figures,

48
00:02:34,914 --> 00:02:39,230
human approval for anything involving money, role-aware agents, and fifty-three automated tests,

49
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:41,181
including the Muse Spark tool-calling path.

50
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,821
Next: live sales and bank feeds,

51
00:02:43,861 --> 00:02:47,232
orders sent straight to suppliers, and verified payroll packs.

52
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:53,600
Detect. Prepare. You approve. That's Beezy. Thanks for watching.
